    "background_story": "Arleth was a brilliant and devout Talmudic scholar who spent most of her life studying the ancient texts. Her specialty was the Mishna, the oral traditions of Jewish law and ethics. Arleth's love for the Mishna began when she was a young girl, listening to her father's stories about the wise rabbis who compiled the teachings. As she delved deeper into her studies, she became known for her insightful commentary and ability to apply the ancient wisdom to modern life. Arleth's dedication to the Mishna led her to write a groundbreaking book that explored the parallels between the ancient text and contemporary social justice issues. Her work earned her recognition as a leading expert in the field, and she was sought after by scholars and community leaders from around the world.",
